---
code: K0031
title: Bad Static Assert
severity: ERROR
since: 0.1.0
category: parse
deprecated: False
tags: [parse, syntax, static-assert, compile-time]
description: "'static-assert' arguments are missing or malformed"
---

A `static-assert` statement must be written as `static-assert(condition)` or `static-assert(condition, "message")`, where the first argument is a boolean expression and the optional second argument is a plain string literal.

## Example

This error occurs when `static-assert` omits its parentheses, has no condition expression, passes a non-string message, or supplies extra arguments:

```kura
static-assert

static-assert(1 == 1, 42)
```

## Solution

Provide a valid condition expression inside parentheses, optionally followed by a plain string diagnostic message:

```kura
static-assert(1 == 1)

static-assert(max-items > 0, "max-items must be positive")
```
